# Disable the ARM64 EFI/EFI-stub so the generated Image is a plain, non-EFI
# ARM64 kernel image (no "MZ" PE stub, entry_offset 0), matching the layout
# of the known-good pmOS 6.3.1 v74/v100 images that the OnePlus 3 LK
# bootloader successfully boots.
#
# Linux v7.2 upstream defaults CONFIG_EFI=y ("UEFI runtime support", see
# arch/arm64/Kconfig), which selects EFI_STUB and EFI_GENERIC_STUB and turns
# the built Image into an EFI application (starts with the "MZ" PE header and
# entry_offset = 0x4000).  The OnePlus 3 MSM8996 has no UEFI firmware; its LK
# bootloader boots a plain ARM64 Image (entry_offset = 0).  Booting the
# EFI-stub Image from the wrong entry point fails before any kernel output,
# which is observed as an immediate return to fastboot.
#
# The known-good pmOS 6.3.1 images have "# CONFIG_EFI is not set", hence the
# same non-EFI plain Image format.
#
# This is applied together with oneplus3-vabits48.fragment so the A/B keeps
# every other variable identical to OP3-BOOT-015.
# CONFIG_EFI is not set
